.TH ZERODDS-MQTT-BRIDGED 1 "" "ZeroDDS" "ZeroDDS Manual"
.SH NAME
zerodds-mqtt-bridged \- DDS to MQTT 5 bridge daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zerodds-mqtt-bridged
[\fB\-\-config\fR \fIFILE\fR]
[\fB\-\-broker\fR \fIURL\fR]
[\fB\-\-domain\fR \fIID\fR]
[\fB\-\-topic\fR \fIDDS:MQTT\fR]...
[\fB\-\-log\-level\fR \fILEVEL\fR]
[\fB\-V\fR | \fB\-h\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B zerodds-mqtt-bridged
mirrors DDS topics to MQTT 5 broker topics and vice versa. Implements
.IR docs/specs/zerodds-mqtt-bridge-1.0.md .
Talks to any MQTT 5 broker (Mosquitto, EMQX, HiveMQ) over TCP/TLS,
MQTT 3.1.1 as a compatibility mode,
retries the broker at start and after a lost connection with exponential
back-off
.RB ( mqtt.reconnect ;
a connection the broker ended with DISCONNECT 0x8E Session taken over is
tried again after
.BR max_delay_ms ),
supports per-topic MQTT QoS (0/1/2), Retain, Message Expiry Interval,
Content Type and user properties, and one participant and broker
connection per tenant.
.PP
The log is JSON on stdout, one object per line with
.BR timestamp ,
.BR level ,
.BR event
and the fields of the event
.RB ( mqtt_topic ,
.BR dds_topic ,
.BR bytes ,
.BR mqtt_qos ,
.BR latency_us ,
.BR connect_state ,
.BR tenant ,
\&...), written when its level reaches
.BR log_level ;
an error that ends the start goes to stderr as well.
On Linux the daemon integrates with
.BR systemd (1)
via Type=notify; on macOS with
.BR launchd (8);
on Windows it runs as service
.BR ZeroDDSMQTTBridge .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-config =\fIFILE\fR
The config file (YAML), with drop-ins in its sibling
.IR FILE .d/.
Without it the system file is read when it exists:
.I /etc/zerodds/mqtt-bridged.yaml
with
.I /etc/zerodds/mqtt-bridged.d/
(on macOS under
.IR /usr/local/etc/zerodds );
without that file the built-in defaults apply.
See
.BR zerodds-mqtt-bridged.yaml (5).
.TP
.BR \-\-broker =\fIURL\fR
MQTT broker URL
.RI ( mqtt:// ", " mqtts:// ", " ws:// ", " wss:// ).
.TP
.BR \-\-client\-id =\fIID\fR
MQTT client ID. Default:
.IR zerodds-bridge-<host> .
.TP
.BR \-\-domain =\fIID\fR
DDS domain ID. Default: 0.
.TP
.BR \-\-username =\fIUSER\fR
MQTT username.
.TP
.BR \-\-password =\fIPASS\fR
MQTT password.
.TP
.BR \-\-tls\-ca =\fIFILE\fR
CA cert.
.TP
.BR \-\-tls\-cert =\fIFILE\fR
Client cert.
.TP
.BR \-\-tls\-key =\fIFILE\fR
Client key.
.TP
.BR \-\-topic =\fIDDS:MQTT\fR
Topic override (repeatable).
.TP
.BR \-\-log\-level =\fILEVEL\fR
Override log level. One of
.IR trace ", " debug ", " info ", " warn ", " error .
.TP
.BR \-\-metrics =\fIADDR\fR
Prometheus listen addr; the families
.B zerodds_mqtt_bridge_*
of
.BR zerodds-mqtt-bridged.yaml (5)
.BR metrics .
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Version info.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show the option synopsis.
.TP
.BR \-\-set " \fIPATH\fR=\fIVALUE\fR"
One setting above every file, repeatable;
.BI + PATH = VALUE
appends to a list.
.TP
.B \-\-check\-config
Validate and print the effective configuration with the origin of every
value, then exit: 0 valid, 1 invalid value or unknown key, 2 unreadable
file, syntax error or include cycle.
.SH SIGNALS
.B SIGTERM
graceful shutdown,
.B SIGHUP
reads the configuration again: the topic ACL and the subject apply from
then on, a withdrawn right stops the samples of that topic at once;
sessions persist. The credentials of
.B auth
apply to the next broker connection when
.B auth.mode
and
.B auth.enhanced.method
stay; when they changed, a connection with enhanced authentication
re-authenticates with them (MQTT 5.0 AUTH 0x19), a reload that keeps them
sends no AUTH. The broker TLS material
.RB ( mqtt.tls.ca_file ,
.BR cert_file ,
.BR key_file ,
read again), the server name and the ALPN offer apply to the next broker
connection; the connection that stands keeps its own. TLS material that
does not load refuses the reload. Changed topics, broker address or client
id,
.BR mqtt.tls.enabled ,
auth mode or method or domain need a restart and are logged; a changed
.B log_level
applies at once. A configuration that does not load changes nothing.
.SH WINDOWS SERVICE
Started by the service control manager, the daemon runs as the service
.BR ZeroDDSMQTTBridge :
start pending until it serves, then running; the stop and shutdown
controls are SIGTERM,
.B sc.exe control ZeroDDSMQTTBridge paramchange
is SIGHUP; when it ends, the service is stopped with the exit status below.
The service has no stdout: its log is appended to
.I %PROGRAMDATA%\eZeroDDS\elogs\emqtt\-bridged.log
(C:\eProgramData when the variable is not set); a file that cannot be
opened ends the start with exit status 1.
Started from a console, Ctrl+C, Ctrl+Break and the closing of the console
are SIGTERM, and the log stays on stdout.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT
Optional OTLP endpoint, such as http://localhost:4318. When it is set, the
daemon sends OTLP/HTTP/JSON spans to its
.I /v1/traces
every 5 s and at the end of a shutdown: one trace per PUBLISH roundtrip,
the root
.B mqtt.publish
(a PUBLISH of the daemon until the broker's PUBACK or PUBCOMP, from the
sample or, for the replay buffer after a reconnect, from the replay; or a
PUBLISH of the broker until its handling ended) with the child
.B dds.write
for each DDS write of a PUBLISH of the broker. A PUBLISH of the daemon has
no
.BR dds.write ;
the catalog, the reports and what a resumed session sends again are no
span.
.TP
.B MQTT_PASSWORD
The broker password; the setting
.BR mqtt.password ,
above the files, below
.BR \-\-set .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Normal shutdown (SIGTERM/SIGINT, also while the start connects).
.TP
.B 1
Configuration error, also auth settings that do not fit their mode (an
anonymous
.B none
towards a broker not on the loopback interface, for example), a
.B mqtt.session_dir
the daemon cannot create or write, or a session state another process
holds.
.TP
.B 2
Broker connect error: not reachable within
.B mqtt.connect_timeout_secs
(also a broker that does not answer the TLS handshake in time or closes
the connection during it), or a CONNACK refusal other than those of 5.
.TP
.B 3
DDS discovery error.
.TP
.B 4
TLS error: TLS material that does not load
.RB ( mqtt.tls.ca_file ", " cert_file ", " key_file ),
or a refused handshake: the broker's certificate is not trusted or not for
its name, or no common protocol.
.TP
.B 5
Authentication error: CONNACK 0x86, 0x87, 0x8A or 0x8C; MQTT 3.1.1 return
code 4 or 5; an enhanced authentication whose client side fails (a SCRAM
server signature that does not verify).
.SH FILES
.I /etc/zerodds/mqtt-bridged.yaml ", " /var/log/zerodds/mqtt-bridged.log ", " /var/lib/zerodds/mqtt-bridge/ .
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zerodds-mqtt-bridged.yaml (5),
.BR mosquitto (8).
.SH STANDARDS
MQTT v5 (OASIS), DDS 1.4, RTPS 2.5.
